Xbox Help
Game Help was a last-minute project with severe design constraints. Xbox One was months from shipping and a help system had been promised for snap on the console but had not been built. I quickly scoped the project for technical and design constraints and devised a system that would scale for both the writing staff who would need to provide the content and game developers who would plug in their manuals for games.

Xbox Clubs
Xbox Clubs is a cross-platform (Mobile, PC and console) feature combining current constructs in Xbox: people and games, and combined them together to create clubs. Clubs allow users to create their own public or private clubs, set their own social standards for behavior, engage in chat and arrange gameplay sessions. One of the biggest problems is online multiplayer gaming is negative experiences from culture clashes, enabling users to create and police their own culture and clubs will result in longer playtime, higher satisfaction and more social engagement. This project is still ongoing this is a sample of work-in-progress.

